{"_doc": "Committed expected values for the citation-drift gate. Per the PROTOCOL Gate standard: the frozen-run baseline pins the digest of every snapshot input file, and the self-test's expected exit codes and finding ids live here rather than in the script, so the expected values are independent of the recomputation.", "frozen_run": {"revision": "679af5d749f2fd48b9d543e3c99d348d5458f90f", "note": "the revision the committed verdict was measured against; a run over a different revision is a different measurement", "verdict": "failed", "expected_findings": ["citation_dead"]}, "snapshots": {"config-toml-landmarks": "387e1f082dda6e77f5ea63677b15f67aef7d49d8820dc8d140a62c0d1096f154"}, "selftest": [{"case": "clean", "exit_code": 0, "finding": "citations_clean"}, {"case": "dead", "exit_code": 1, "finding": "citation_dead"}, {"case": "out_of_range", "exit_code": 1, "finding": "citation_out_of_range"}, {"case": "file_absent", "exit_code": 1, "finding": "citation_file_absent"}, {"case": "moved", "exit_code": 1, "finding": "citation_moved"}, {"case": "stamped", "exit_code": 0, "finding": "citation_historical_ok"}, {"case": "no_snapshot_dir", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "pointer_table_unreadable"}, {"case": "snapshot_missing", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "snapshot_missing"}, {"case": "snapshot_tampered", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "snapshot_tampered"}, {"case": "table_unreadable", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "pointer_table_unreadable"}, {"case": "rev_unresolvable", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "revision_unresolvable"}, {"case": "table_tampered", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "table_tampered"}, {"case": "table_absent", "exit_code": 2, "finding": "pointer_table_unreadable"}], "table_sha256": "738b3a569fb7dc96e1097de0121a19d86856fb8de43030a8cba0394428dd6e3f"}